VERSION:   4
COMMENT: epsilon-iron (Fe), hcp, P6_3/mmc - Miozzi et al. (2020) Minerals 10, 100, doi:10.3390/min10020100
COMMENT: 3rd order Birch-Murnaghan isotherm at 300 K of the thermal fit (preferred solution): V0=22.81 A3 (6.87(2) cm3/mol), K0=129(1) GPa, K0P=6.24(4)
COMMENT: Thermal model of the source: Mie-Gruneisen-Debye, thetaD=420 K (fixed), gamma0=1.11(1), q=0.3(3), reference 300 K, fitted between 30 and 140 GPa, 300 and 3400 K (MgO scale of Speziale et al. 2001)
COMMENT: ALPHAT, DALPHADT, DK0DT, DK0PDT fitted on this model (thermal pressure, as in Dioptas) between 30 and 140 GPa and 300 and 3400 K: pressure within 0.11 GPa, temperature within 15 K
COMMENT: Alternative fit with the data of Dewaele et al. (2006): V0=22.57 A3, K0=153(1) GPa, K0P=5.39(4), gamma0=1.09(1), q=0.26(4)
COMMENT: epsilon-Fe is stable above about 16 GPa: V0 is an extrapolation
COMMENT: Extrapolated above 140 GPa: 209 GPa for the volume measured at 197 GPa (300 K, He medium) by Dewaele et al. (2006)
COMMENT: c/a=1.603 read on the inset of Fig. 1 of Dewaele et al. (2006) Phys. Rev. Lett. 97, 215504, doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.97.215504, at 20 GPa; c/a decreases to 1.597 at 150-200 GPa, not described by the EoS
COMMENT: Intensities calculated (Cu Ka, Cromer-Mann form factor of Cl used for Fe, no thermal factor)
